author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "Every supported non-test export from declared SDK subpaths is reachable from the aggregate barrel or appears in an explicit reviewed exclusion contract with a reason; docs match runtime truth; a derived negative-control gate fails when a subpath-only export is introduced; packed Node and Bun consumers compile representative query, contracts, governance, and runtime imports from the documented aggregate."
goal: project management = context management
objective: The aggregate SDK entrypoint is a truthful compatibility surface
parent: pm-usfg
resolution: Derived aggregate completeness gate and explicit exclusion contract shipped.
expected_result: Every supported SDK subpath export is available from the documented aggregate or explicitly excluded with rationale.
actual_result: "Aggregate exposes 954 supported symbols, reports zero missing exports, and the packed consumer plus negative-control gate pass."
